  "id": "clance-impostor-phenomenon-scale",
  "term": "Clance Impostor Phenomenon Scale",
  "definition": "The Clance Impostor Phenomenon Scale is a self-report assessment used in research to measure trait impostor phenomenon, a pattern of feeling intellectually or professionally fraudulent despite evidence of success. It is one of the measures used to study impostorism and its psychometric properties have been reviewed in the assessment literature.",
